  <section|Exact construction audit><label|exact-construction-audit>

  <verbatim|bairn> fixes the finite frame family
  <math|F=<around|(|<math-up|frames><space|0.17em>G|)>.<math-up|level><space|0.17em>d>,
  its test list, <math|e=<math-up|title><around|(|P<rsub|1>|)>>,
  <math|a=<math-up|title><around|(|P<rsub|0>|)>>, credibility <math|h>, door
  rate <math|\<nu\>>, and

  <\equation*>
    c=<math-up|orbitCost><around|(|F|)><space|0.17em><math-up|errorPrice><around|(|<math-up|hol><space|0.17em>G,F|)><space|0.17em><math-up|corn><around|(|G,d|)>*<space|0.17em>a.
  </equation*>

  It sets <math|Z=<math-up|testPrice><around|(|F|)>\<geqslant\>1>,
  <math|T=<math-up|readPrice><around|(|F|)>\<geqslant\>1>, and
  <math|\<kappa\>=min <around|(|<around|(|\<nu\>/2|)>/<around|(|c*Z|)>,\<zeta\>|)>>.
  For each probe <math|p>, the charged scalar is

  <\equation*>
    g<rsub|p><around|(|s|)>=<math-up|partPrice><around|(|<math-up|hol><space|0.17em>G,p|)><space|0.17em><math-up|gaugeMeter><around|(|d|)>*L<rsup|d>*<space|0.17em>2*<around|(|e*s+s|)>+s.
  </equation*>

  Each <math|g<rsub|p>> is continuous at zero with
  <math|g<rsub|p><around|(|0|)>=0>. <verbatim|V.eventually_all> over the
  finite test family gives a common open ball radius <math|b\<gtr\>0> on
  which all the finitely many inequalities
  <math|g<rsub|p><around|(|s|)>\<leqslant\>\<kappa\>> hold. The source sets
  <math|Q=b/2>.

  The proof then combines the following exact source outputs on one eventual
  tail:

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|Mercury.tuned> supplies <math|u> with strict-power rate
    <math|-1/2> and <verbatim|PermitY>. If there is no branch patch,
    <math|u=0> and the permit statement is vacuous. Otherwise it applies
    <verbatim|trove> to that actual branch patch and replaces its response
    <math|f> by <math|2<around|\||f|\|>>; the rate is unchanged and the
    absolute value preserves the purchased permit bound.

    <item><verbatim|highstar> at tolerance <math|Q> gives the local
    probe-to-run error, after multiplication by <math|L<rsup|d>>.

    <item><verbatim|scales_m> is called with price <math|Q/e> and its
    linear-in-<math|t> bound is evaluated at <math|t=e>, giving the cap
    <math|\<leqslant\>1> and clock/moment bound <math|Q/\<chi\>>.

    <item><verbatim|Blush.fruition>, with coefficient <math|L<rsup|d>> and
    budget <math|S=<around|(|\<nu\>/2|)>/<around|(|c*T*h|)>>, gives the cloud
    mass bound.

    <item><verbatim|Rebuild.geometry> gives the two threshold ratios required
    for the factor-two blend.
  </enumerate>

  The source has <math|\<chi\>\<in\>\<cal-R\><rsub|0>> and
  <math|u\<in\>\<cal-R\><rsub|-1/2>>, so the product-rate rule gives
  <math|\<chi\>*u\<in\>\<cal-R\><rsub|-1/2>> and hence
  <math|\<chi\><around|\||u|\|>\<to\>0> by the strict-power definition. The
  manuscript then carries out the remaining algebra: cap and path bounds are
  already <math|Q/\<chi\>>; the law follows from
  <math|g<rsub|p><around|(|Q|)>\<leqslant\>\<kappa\>>; and the combined
  cloud/probe charge is at most <math|c*<around|(|Z*\<kappa\>+T*S*h|)>\<leqslant\>\<nu\>>.

  <section|Canonical proof reuse and exact
  match><label|canonical-proof-reuse-and-exact-match>

  The branch-case local insertion is the fixed-insertion linear comparison in
  the canonical <verbatim|principal-gaussian-comparison.tex> (reviewed
  fingerprint <verbatim|ac21f608d8f153fa88222a602629caddf8b6303c343f709f087ddf0fc211ee1c>)
  and its primitive mean/covariance comparison in
  <verbatim|principal-comparison-jets.tex> (reviewed fingerprint
  <verbatim|ff624cbd11db727d32b9c3c50cf5540d2a048efb46e3e83b6c05c8b64dd1dded>).
  Their review log explicitly identifies the
  <verbatim|Mercury.wickets>/<verbatim|trove> route and records bounded
  passes under the displayed hypotheses.

  The exact match is: the fixed insertion is <verbatim|golf>, with amplitude
  <math|\<tau\>=M.<math-up|weight>>; its regular masked ingredient is
  <math|L<rprime|'>=M.<math-up|ingredient>>; <verbatim|H.supportP> confines
  the read support to the selected protected region; the local field is the
  journey <math|y\<mapsto\><math-up|journey><around|(|X.*V,j,U<around|(|y|)>|)>>
  with <math|j\<leqslant\>n> and the prescribed normalized directional/canopy
  bounds. Forest, tags, local read set, and insertion mask are fixed during
  differentiation. The comparison's <math|h<around|(|z|)>> is this same
  masked insertion, so <math|<around|\||h|\|>\<leqslant\>\<tau\>> and no
  derivative falls on <math|h>. The actual and reference integrals are the
  two normalized Gaussian integrals in equations (5)--(7) of the manuscript.
  The source identities <verbatim|pop6> and <verbatim|pop9> identify them
  with the local actual and reference observables. The comparison estimate
  gives ordered derivatives through order <math|n>; the sector and reference
  covariance/mean hypotheses are discharged by the separately reviewed
  primitive comparison section. The common compact coordinate support and
  cutoff-one region come from the protected compensation; outside the finite
  local price ball the cutoff factors vanish. The finite price-radius
  integration uses the actual cloud generated from the local covariance, the
  <verbatim|corridor> estimate, and the <verbatim|silence> cutoff. It yields
  a derivative bound: for every <math|r\<leqslant\>n>, the norm of the
  <math|r>th derivative at the chart origin is at most the common price. This
  is the estimate used in the permit conclusion.

  The remaining rate assembly in <verbatim|trove> is explicit:
  <verbatim|spicules> and <verbatim|weave> choose the local rate-zero and
  half-rate budgets; <verbatim|sweaters> supplies the score and
  protected-chart bounds; <verbatim|blends> combines them with
  <verbatim|incomingE> and the positive slice exponential and proves strict
  rate <math|-1/2>. <verbatim|Riddle.tuned> then handles the no-patch case by
  zero and the branch case by <math|2<around|\||f|\|>>. This is the actual
  source route, not an additional assumption in the local insertion
  comparison. The finite-probe selection and scalar price algebra are the new
  proof in this unit. Read-only commands used in this stage: <verbatim|rg -n>
  on the named declarations; <verbatim|sed -n> over
  <verbatim|Quince/Bairn.lean>, <verbatim|Cub/Chant.lean>,
  <verbatim|Mercury/Riddle.lean>, <verbatim|Mercury/Radio.lean>,
  <verbatim|Mercury/Lagoon.lean>, <verbatim|Quince/Pix.lean>,
  <verbatim|Quince/Dawn.lean>, <verbatim|Quince/Grade.lean>,
  <verbatim|Brim/Heights.lean>, <verbatim|Brim/Sun.lean>,
  <verbatim|Brim/Symbols.lean>, <verbatim|Brim/Weld.lean>,
  <verbatim|Baffle/Furl.lean>, and <verbatim|Blush/Little.lean>. I ran
  <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py>; it stopped because the
  isolated clone lacks the parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>.
  No Lean or TeX build was run.

